abstract:
No public Level 2 microstructure dataset exists for Kalshi’s prediction markets. I describe a method for collecting, 
&lt;br&gt;
 then reconstructing every tick of every full-depth limit order book on Kalshi using their public, free API. First, the system collects Kalshi’s WebSocket data streams, anchored by periodic REST API snapshots (Section 3). Then, the reconstruction algorithm—snapshot-anchored windowing with sequential delta replay—uses q to process these streams into a partitioned KDB+ time-series database of tick-level LOB states for every market on Kalshi (Section 5). The method is replicable by anyone with access to Kalshi’s public API. I also document implementation challenges specific to KDB+/q that required non-standard reconstruction patterns. I report aggregate dataset characteristics and discuss what this infrastructure enables for prediction market research.
